1
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,370
It's been ten days now.

2
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:17,740
I'm so glad I came out here.

3
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:23,000
Lord Dias helped me build
a new yurt for my own use.

4
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:28,250
He also gave me this spear and armor,
both made from dragon materials.

5
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:34,750
Lord Dias has bestowed on me such gifts
I'm not sure even royalty could obtain.

6
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:38,080
I must honor his trust in me.

7
00:02:10,010 --> 00:02:12,480
Today we're having
herb-roasted black ghee.

8
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:15,480
Klaus, you're in for a treat!

9
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:21,380
How incredibly delicious!

10
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:24,110
You'll make a fine wife, Lady Alna.

11
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:25,950
Right, Lord Dias?

12
00:02:26,610 --> 00:02:27,790
Uh-huh...

13
00:02:30,210 --> 00:02:30,920
Huh?

14
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:34,530
Feel free to have more, Klaus.

15
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:36,480
Thank you so much!

16
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,170
Please join me, Lord Dias.

17
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:43,600
You know, I don't think being called
"lord" is ever going to sound right to me.

18
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:47,810
I must in order to make
our positions clear!

19
00:02:50,790 --> 00:02:55,200
He says, "We contribute
to the herd by providing wool."

20
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:58,820
"You be a man who's useful, too."

21
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:01,940
As captain of this domain's forces,
I will do my best

22
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:04,070
to live up to Francis's expectations!

23
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:08,010
Klaus is the currently the
entirety of said forces,

24
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:06,500
Okay!

25
00:03:06,890 --> 00:03:09,170
I don't know what you said, but thank you!

26
00:03:08,010 --> 00:03:10,830
but I guess enthusiasm
makes up for the rest.

27
00:03:13,970 --> 00:03:15,990
Is something headed our way?

28
00:03:15,990 --> 00:03:20,090
Yes, from the east. Twelve.

29
00:03:20,610 --> 00:03:22,330
They're all human, but...

30
00:03:25,990 --> 00:03:31,450
One of the twelve people she sensed
appears to be weak, on the verge of death.

31
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:33,830
I'll go investigate before it's too late.

32
00:03:34,190 --> 00:03:35,620
Shall I accompany you?

33
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:37,700
No, you hold down the fort.

34
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:41,360
If anything about them seems off,
I'll send Alna and the baars home.

35
00:03:41,590 --> 00:03:44,870
At that point, I want you
to protect everyone here.

36
00:03:45,290 --> 00:03:46,470
You can count on me.

37
00:03:46,850 --> 00:03:47,370
That I do.

38
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:53,710
That magic is incredible.

39
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:56,380
The royal capital is to the east.

40
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:58,870
Right now in the city,

41
00:03:58,870 --> 00:04:02,300
the five princes and princesses are
in the grips of a succession dispute.

42
00:04:02,950 --> 00:04:05,400
Princess Diane from the other day

43
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:07,890
has less military might
than her siblings' factions,

44
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:11,140
so I'm sure she was trying
to court Lord Dias.

45
00:04:11,570 --> 00:04:14,400
The fact that he never received his reward

46
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:18,290
must be because the second prince, said
to be a money grubber, appropriated it.

47
00:04:19,070 --> 00:04:22,370
The nobility is split into factions,
and the effects of their

48
00:04:22,770 --> 00:04:25,370
bickering and schemes are felt
even out on the frontier.

49
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:34,980
Someday, the conflict itself
might make its way here.

50
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:41,420
But to fight and die in Lord Dias's
service wouldn't be so bad.

51
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,090
They're back already?

52
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,890
An herbal infusion.

53
00:04:52,890 --> 00:04:54,600
Thank you.

54
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:57,060
Drinking that will help with fatigue.

55
00:05:01,890 --> 00:05:03,360
Thank you.

56
00:05:03,890 --> 00:05:05,530
They were driven out?

57
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:09,370
Yeah. There was a rebellion
in a neighboring domain,

58
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,620
leading a destitute village

59
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:14,620
to expel the elderly women
so they'd have fewer to feed.

60
00:05:14,890 --> 00:05:16,380
A neighboring domain?

61
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:19,630
That's most likely Kasdeks.

62
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:24,760
I passed through it on the way here,
and they were in dire straits.

63
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:27,510
I'm impressed with these women, though.

64
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:31,630
Grandma Maya over there
is their de facto leader.

65
00:05:31,630 --> 00:05:35,020
She used her fortunetelling skills
to find a way to survive,

66
00:05:35,350 --> 00:05:37,620
which is how they ended up here.

67
00:05:38,230 --> 00:05:39,920
We've done it, Klaus!

68
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:40,520
Huh?

69
00:05:41,150 --> 00:05:44,280
We got twelve new subjects all at once!

70
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:47,330
Of course he'd say that.

71
00:05:48,850 --> 00:05:50,920
Better build some more yurts.

72
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,410
L-Lord Dias!

73
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:57,160
Treat the refugees as you see fit,
but they won't contribute much—

74
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:59,900
That's another way they're amazing!

75
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:05,050
All those ladies are over seventy,
and Grandma Maya is ninety!

76
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:08,340
I hope they can teach us
the secret of a long life!

77
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:10,300
He's not even listening.

78
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:12,370
I agree with him.

79
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:15,560
Dias is the lord here, after all.

80
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:21,350
They're saying we should
abide by Dias's decision,

81
00:06:21,350 --> 00:06:23,940
as he's the strongest of the herd.

82
00:06:23,940 --> 00:06:27,190
Gotta hurry and get these yurts
built for the elderly women!

83
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:33,950
That's right.
He's always been like this.

84
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:40,240
I'm afraid we must withdraw!

85
00:06:41,270 --> 00:06:43,400
We're going to run without fighting?!

86
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:46,260
There's a large enemy force
right on our doorstep!

87
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:49,840
Who's going to protect the citizens
still in the evacuation shelter?!

88
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:50,950
Quiet, you!

89
00:06:50,950 --> 00:06:52,090
Move out!

90
00:06:52,990 --> 00:06:56,690
And you call yourselves
soldiers of the kingdom?!

91
00:07:00,090 --> 00:07:01,640
Enemy soldiers already?!

92
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:04,610
Damn it! Is there where I meet my end?

93
00:07:04,610 --> 00:07:07,480
Hey! Klaus!

94
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:08,990
Sir Dias!

95
00:07:08,990 --> 00:07:10,490
Where have you been?

96
00:07:10,490 --> 00:07:15,990
I heard a child crying, so I went
to look, and sure enough...

97
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:21,010
Sorry. I need you to take this boy, too.

98
00:07:21,010 --> 00:07:22,500
Don't leave me here!

99
00:07:22,730 --> 00:07:25,960
I'm scared! Don't go!

100
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:29,100
I'm not going anywhere.

101
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:32,760
I promise to protect you,
so be patient here a little while.

102
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:41,020
Klaus.

103
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:43,270
Don't die on me.

104
00:07:45,390 --> 00:07:46,090
Got it.

105
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:53,360
I don't clearly remember
what happened after that.

106
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:57,870
I thought only of keeping the enemy
away from that shelter...

107
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:03,110
and how I was going to help him.

108
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:07,330
I was sure it was the best strategy
I had in that fight.

109
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:25,360
He hasn't changed at all since then.

110
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:28,400
Not even now, as a domain lord.

111
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,900
I've been a fool.

112
00:08:31,670 --> 00:08:34,190
I thought I'd be great
and honorable by dying.

113
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:37,750
I need to live and give him my support...

114
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:41,840
He's earnestly trying
to become a great lord.

115
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:44,710
Hang on there.

116
00:08:44,710 --> 00:08:46,670
You'll end up damaging the yurt.

117
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:48,900
Let me lend you a hand!

118
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:06,160
Thank you for building a meeting place.

119
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:10,420
We shall use this this space
to work as well.

120
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:15,530
They said when the baar wool piles up,
they'll spin yarn and make cloth.

121
00:09:15,530 --> 00:09:17,390
That'll be helpful.

122
00:09:20,650 --> 00:09:23,500
Why the grave face?

123
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:29,440
Well, with more people here now, I was
thinking of declaring this a village.

124
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:31,300
I just can't think of a good name.

125
00:09:31,580 --> 00:09:33,790
Let's make it Dias Village.

126
00:09:33,790 --> 00:09:35,800
It can't be named after me.

127
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:39,710
I think Dragon Slayer Village would work!

128
00:09:39,710 --> 00:09:40,850
Rejected.

129
00:09:42,170 --> 00:09:44,560
How about Iluk Village?

130
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,110
Iluk Village?

131
00:09:46,110 --> 00:09:49,720
It means "first village"
in the ancient tongue.

132
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:51,110
Makes sense, right?

133
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,700
Iluk...

134
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:54,720
Iluk Village, eh?

135
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,170
That settles it.

136
00:10:05,290 --> 00:10:06,890
Meeting adjourned, then!

137
00:10:07,290 --> 00:10:09,290
What a nice name.

138
00:10:09,290 --> 00:10:10,790
I'll say.

139
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:15,890
Dias, we have ourselves a village.
Now we need more subjects.

140
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:16,800
Yeah.

141
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:20,550
But as for what Grandma Maya suggested...

142
00:10:20,770 --> 00:10:23,060
You called, young Dias?

143
00:10:24,090 --> 00:10:26,560
Or at least, I had a hunch you had.

144
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:29,440
I didn't say a thing out loud.

145
00:10:29,820 --> 00:10:33,570
By the way, regarding
we were discussing earlier...

146
00:10:33,970 --> 00:10:39,940
If you want more subjects, you can sell
those dragon materials and buy slaves.

147
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:41,770
Why not just do that?

148
00:10:43,030 --> 00:10:45,330
I hate slavery.

149
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:48,960
I saw enslaved soldiers on the
battlefield a number of times,

150
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:52,210
and they were all treated horribly.

151
00:10:52,890 --> 00:10:58,360
I intend to prohibit the owning and
selling of slaves within my domain.

152
00:11:02,650 --> 00:11:06,970
Good. We don't care for slavery either.

153
00:11:06,970 --> 00:11:08,230
Huh?!

154
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,840
Then why did you...

155
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:12,190
I wanted to know how you really felt.

156
00:11:12,190 --> 00:11:16,480
Had you been on board with it,
I would have steered you away.

157
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:22,860
Do forgive me. There are just
too many tragic tales from our land.

158
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:26,200
You mean Kasdeks?

159
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:27,200
Yes.

160
00:11:28,050 --> 00:11:31,630
The lord and his eldest son
enjoy hunting down slaves.

161
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,340
And his second son, the one
who picked a fight with them,

162
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:39,340
is said to have many
female slaves attend him.

163
00:11:39,730 --> 00:11:43,260
This domain and Iluk Village
won't go down that road.

164
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:45,170
I won't allow it.

165
00:11:52,930 --> 00:11:56,050
A traveling merchant comes by
the onikin village periodically,

166
00:11:56,050 --> 00:11:59,780
and I sent word for him
to swing by here as well.

167
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:02,530
I wonder what he's like.

168
00:12:10,270 --> 00:12:12,290
A frog?!

169
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:15,150
Hop!

170
00:12:15,790 --> 00:12:19,460
You mus' be that
Dragon Slayer feller, huh!

171
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:22,800
Mah name's Peijin-Do.

172
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:25,550
Let's do some nice business togetha, yah?

173
00:12:26,030 --> 00:12:28,310
He's a member of the frogkin race.

174
00:12:28,310 --> 00:12:30,560
He's a frogman!

175
00:12:30,990 --> 00:12:32,480
Let's get down to it.

176
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:35,690
Reckon I could take a gander
at them earth dragon materials?

177
00:12:37,270 --> 00:12:39,910
White, so no hostility...

178
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:41,900
Here we are.

179
00:12:43,530 --> 00:12:45,070
Is there a problem?

180
00:12:45,070 --> 00:12:46,630
N-Nuh-uh!

181
00:12:46,630 --> 00:12:49,200
I was just expectin' somethin' smaller.

182
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:54,460
If you'll excuse me bein' impolite,
did ya really kill it by yer lonesome?

183
00:12:57,180 --> 00:13:01,680
He wants to know his trading
partner isn't lying to him.

184
00:13:10,010 --> 00:13:13,230
There it is! The Dragon Shell Crusher!

185
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:17,230
Now do you believe me?

186
00:13:17,230 --> 00:13:19,770
Y-Y-You betcha I do!

187
00:13:19,770 --> 00:13:21,910
Happy to trade witcha!

188
00:13:21,910 --> 00:13:24,700
You guys, get to unloadin'!

189
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:25,780
Y-Yessir!

190
00:13:26,070 --> 00:13:27,530
Hup.

191
00:13:27,530 --> 00:13:31,300
Good, good! Glad we got
enough to trade with.

192
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:34,550
I know! Now's a good time
to bring out you-know-what.

193
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:37,960
We couldn't offload 'em
in the Beastkin Nation,

194
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:42,100
but yer a human, Mr. Dias.
I bet you'll take 'em.

195
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,990
The light has vanished from their eyes.

196
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:53,700
They must be orphans, like me.

197
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:57,060
So Peijin is selling orphans?

198
00:13:57,310 --> 00:13:58,810
As slaves?!

199
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:01,910
Calm down.

200
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:03,440
Alna...

201
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:08,720
Don't make such a scary face
in front of children, young Dias.

202
00:14:09,370 --> 00:14:13,950
I'm sorry, but we do not
wish to purchase slaves.

203
00:14:13,950 --> 00:14:15,950
Y-Ya got it all wrong!

204
00:14:16,250 --> 00:14:17,950
These two ain't slaves!

205
00:14:17,950 --> 00:14:21,790
If I hadn't taken 'em as merchandise,
they'd be dead, I tell ya!

206
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:24,860
In the village where
these here twins were born,

207
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:28,550
the villagers shunned 'em.
Said they'd bring calamity!

208
00:14:28,810 --> 00:14:32,280
They were gonna execute 'em
after they were born, see?

209
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:36,030
So their parents took 'em and
ran away from the village.

210
00:14:36,030 --> 00:14:38,310
That's around when
I made their acquaintance.

211
00:14:38,310 --> 00:14:44,070
But t'was more than them parents
could handle, and they both took ill.

212
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:47,840
They knew their days were numbered,

213
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:50,820
so they asked me to look after
these here girls.

214
00:14:51,090 --> 00:14:55,220
I said no, seein' as I don't
do charity work.

215
00:14:55,220 --> 00:15:01,460
But then they offered money and said
I could take 'em as merchandise.

216
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:03,920
Couldn't say no after that.

217
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:14,970
But the money's all gone now,
and they're puttin' me in the red!

218
00:15:14,970 --> 00:15:17,590
Please, I don't mean no harm!

219
00:15:19,010 --> 00:15:20,350
He isn't lying.

220
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:24,860
Also, the twins are a strong blue.

221
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:27,740
Fine.

222
00:15:28,090 --> 00:15:30,400
I'll take custody of these two.

223
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:33,870
And I'll pay in materials to cover
what you've spent supporting them.

224
00:15:33,870 --> 00:15:35,870
Ya got yerself a deal, sir!

225
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:56,510
How old are you? Three? Four?

226
00:15:56,510 --> 00:16:00,770
You're both so skinny,
you'd better be ready to eat lots.

227
00:16:01,290 --> 00:16:03,610
My name is Dias.

228
00:16:03,610 --> 00:16:06,020
Could you tell me your names?

229
00:16:09,030 --> 00:16:10,900
What games do you like to play?

230
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:12,650
We could play together.

231
00:16:12,650 --> 00:16:16,030
If you tell me what foods like you,
I'll go get some for you.

232
00:16:16,990 --> 00:16:19,430
Anyway, what are your names?

233
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:24,670
This isn't a very good way
to go about this, but...

234
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:28,300
Oh, I get it! You don't have names, huh?

235
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:30,800
Then I'll go ahead and name you myself.

236
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:34,550
Let's see, what kind
of names would be good?

237
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:37,470
No!

238
00:16:37,470 --> 00:16:38,810
No new names!

239
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:42,640
Then could you tell me yours?

240
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:44,350
Not knowing them makes this hard.

241
00:16:46,620 --> 00:16:48,110
Senai.

242
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,360
Ayhan.

243
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:54,880
Oh, okay! Senai and Ayhan!

244
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,850
Thank you for telling me.

245
00:16:56,850 --> 00:16:59,870
You both have such nice, sweet names.

246
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:02,220
All right, Senai and Ayhan.

247
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:05,410
I'd like for you to take a bath with
your new big sister Alna over there

248
00:17:05,410 --> 00:17:07,380
and change your clothes.

249
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:08,630
Could you do that?

250
00:17:13,730 --> 00:17:15,260
Come to me, then.

251
00:17:15,770 --> 00:17:19,140
Later, we'll have some
steamed potatoes for you.

252
00:17:20,420 --> 00:17:22,890
Nice work getting their names out of them.

253
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:28,550
They wanted to protect the names
their beloved parents gave them.

254
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:34,470
I'm surprised by how good you
are with children, Lord Dias.

255
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:38,910
Before the war, I was sort of a
father figure to the other orphans.

256
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:42,910
I hope all of them are doing well.

257
00:17:44,910 --> 00:17:46,550
That's finally taken care of.

258
00:17:47,010 --> 00:17:48,320
Excellent job.

259
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:53,420
Look how clean you are!

260
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:58,880
I can't expect them to
open up right away.

261
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:01,430
For now, it's enough that
I can call them by name.

262
00:18:02,050 --> 00:18:05,050
Those clothes look good
on you, Senai, Ayhan.

263
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:10,190
These aren't human children.

264
00:18:10,530 --> 00:18:14,150
But I get a sense they'll
be good for this place.

265
00:18:14,550 --> 00:18:17,320
I guess I'll watch and see what happens.

266
00:18:19,860 --> 00:18:21,460
This is for you, Senai.

267
00:18:24,730 --> 00:18:26,400
And for you, Ayhan.

268
00:18:29,470 --> 00:18:33,240
Senai, in the ancient tongue,
your name means

269
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:35,420
"one who is beautiful like the moon."

270
00:18:36,190 --> 00:18:40,720
Ayhan, yours means "the holy moon."

271
00:18:41,050 --> 00:18:46,220
Your parents must have had
a deep attachment to the moon.

272
00:18:46,930 --> 00:18:50,980
That's why I'm giving you
these ahi jewels.

273
00:18:51,830 --> 00:18:54,980
It's said the power of the moon
is hidden within them.

274
00:18:55,820 --> 00:18:58,360
"One who is beautiful like the moon"...

275
00:18:58,360 --> 00:19:00,490
"The holy moon"...

276
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:04,630
Senai, Ayhan, we love you.

277
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:09,660
We will always pray for your happiness.

278
00:19:13,420 --> 00:19:18,760
You've both been so brave since
you left your beloved parents.

279
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:21,580
But you don't need to hold back anymore.

280
00:19:21,580 --> 00:19:24,430
When you feel like crying,
go ahead and cry.

281
00:19:27,580 --> 00:19:30,310
They want to comfort the girls, too.

282
00:19:30,310 --> 00:19:33,190
And they say they're good with children.

283
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:42,950
Alna, what is this
ancient tongue you mentioned?

284
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:48,520
An ancient language that exists
only in legends. No one uses it now.

285
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:52,710
I don't know if it's purely
an onikin tradition,

286
00:19:53,370 --> 00:19:56,210
but these two don't seem to be human.

287
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:59,820
It's possible their people once
had contact with the onikin.

288
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:12,500
On this day, Iluk Village grew
a lot more lively and boisterous.

289
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:16,740
And then, ten days later...

290
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:20,640
Senai ate my potato!

291
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:22,570
I said sorry, didn't I?

292
00:20:22,570 --> 00:20:25,150
I was saving it for last!

293
00:20:25,150 --> 00:20:26,780
You can have mine.

294
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:29,240
I don't want your
half-eaten potato, Dias.

295
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:29,920
Huh?

296
00:20:33,540 --> 00:20:35,330
Looks like someone else has arrived.

297
00:20:35,970 --> 00:20:39,610
A lone human on a horse from the east.

298
00:20:40,010 --> 00:20:42,050
I should probably go and see.

299
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:47,000
Being away from you won't be easy,

300
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,960
but right now, they want
to stay close to Senai and Ayhan.

301
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:52,420
All right. Look after both of them.

302
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:56,720
Come back home soon.

303
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,810
We'll be waiting.

304
00:20:58,850 --> 00:21:01,400
Sure. I'll be back before you know it.

305
00:21:05,090 --> 00:21:06,070
Here he comes.

306
00:21:07,820 --> 00:21:10,360
He comes up white. No hostility.

307
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:16,230
Lord Dias, I presume?

308
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:19,710
That's right. Who might you be?

309
00:21:19,710 --> 00:21:23,400
Begging your pardon. I am Kamalotz.

310
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:28,970
I serve Eldan Kasdeks, the new lord
of Kasdeks Domain.

311
00:21:29,350 --> 00:21:31,220
Kasdeks Domain...

312
00:21:31,220 --> 00:21:35,120
Lord Eldan wishes an audience
with you, Lord Dias.

313
00:21:35,120 --> 00:21:37,430
He is on his way as we speak.

314
00:21:37,430 --> 00:21:40,190
Would it be possible
to receive him at your manor—

315
00:21:40,190 --> 00:21:41,290
I'll meet him right here!

316
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:46,490
A-As you say, milord!

317
00:21:48,730 --> 00:21:50,360
A new lord, huh?

318
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:53,560
That must mean the second son's
rebellion was successful.

319
00:21:54,410 --> 00:21:59,980
I'm not letting a guy surrounded by
enslaved women anywhere near Iluk Village.

320
00:22:02,810 --> 00:22:03,500
What's...

321
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:05,560
all that?